<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federal Pact</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Federal Pact was an alliance signed in January 1831 by the Argentine provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, Santa Fe and Entre Ríos against the Unitarian League of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-paz">José María Paz</a>. After Paz was captured and the Unitarians defeated, the other provinces joined it. The pact became the basis of the Argentine Confederation, with Buenos Aires managing foreign relations, and is named in the 1853 constitution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federal-pact.jpg" alt="Federal Pact" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Manuel de Rosas (1793–1877), according to La Gazeta website (vector graphics by Guilherme Paula) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Argentine_Confederation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Federal Pact</b> of 1831 bound the provinces as the Argentine Confederation; fourteen of them later formed the Argentine Republic, while Bolivia, Uruguay and Paraguay went their own ways.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-provinces-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">United Provinces of the Río de la Plata · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Federal Pact</b> of 1831 between Buenos Aires, Santa Fe and Entre Ríos, later joined by the other provinces after the defeat of the Unitarian League, created the Argentine Confederation.</blockquote><a href="/state/argentine-confederation">Argentine Confederation</a></li><li><blockquote>In response, Buenos Aires, Santa Fe and Entre Ríos signed the <b>Federal Pact</b> in January 1831.</blockquote><a href="/state/unitarian-league">Unitarian League</a></li></ul></section>
